{
  "duration": 66.139,
  "phrases": [
    {
      "start": 0.119,
      "end": 0.34,
      "text": "So"
    },
    {
      "start": 0.759,
      "end": 1.74,
      "text": "welcome back again."
    },
    {
      "start": 2.339,
      "end": 4.579,
      "text": "It's time to solve one more problem."
    },
    {
      "start": 5.079,
      "end": 5.879,
      "text": "Now in this problem,"
    },
    {
      "start": 6.379,
      "end": 9.539,
      "text": "a point is thirty meters away from a building."
    },
    {
      "start": 10.059,
      "end": 13.159,
      "text": "From that point, the angle of elevation to the top of the building"
    },
    {
      "start": 13.659,
      "end": 14.739,
      "text": "is thirty degrees."
    },
    {
      "start": 15.259,
      "end": 18.259,
      "text": "The question is asking us to find the height of the building."
    },
    {
      "start": 18.619,
      "end": 21.219,
      "text": "Here, the height of the building is the opposite side,"
    },
    {
      "start": 21.579,
      "end": 25.159,
      "text": "and the thirty meter distance from the building is the adjacent side."
    },
    {
      "start": 25.479,
      "end": 30.42,
      "text": "And we know a trigonometric function that relates with opposite and adjacent side, that is ten."
    },
    {
      "start": 31.179,
      "end": 32.719,
      "text": "Let the height of the building be"
    },
    {
      "start": 33.059,
      "end": 33.639,
      "text": "h meters."
    },
    {
      "start": 34.239,
      "end": 38.04,
      "text": "Using ten ratio, ten theta is equal to opposite by adjacent."
    },
    {
      "start": 38.459,
      "end": 41.359,
      "text": "So ten thirty degrees is equal to h by thirty."
    },
    {
      "start": 41.759,
      "end": 48.539,
      "text": "Now we know ten thirty degrees is equal to one by root three, so we can write one by root three is equal to"
    },
    {
      "start": 48.84,
      "end": 52.139,
      "text": "h by thirty. Now multiply both sides by thirty."
    },
    {
      "start": 52.84,
      "end": 54.619,
      "text": "H is equal to thirty by root three."
    },
    {
      "start": 55.159,
      "end": 56.419,
      "text": "After simplifying this,"
    },
    {
      "start": 57.059,
      "end": 58.68,
      "text": "h is equal to ten root three."
    },
    {
      "start": 59.399,
      "end": 59.779,
      "text": "Hence,"
    },
    {
      "start": 60.319,
      "end": 63.719,
      "text": "the height of the building is ten root three meter."
    },
    {
      "start": 64.279,
      "end": 66.139,
      "text": "So the correct option is option A."
    }
  ],
